# Phase 0: Mochi & Friends

Work from `docs/BUILD_PLAN.md`. One step at a time. Do not start the next step until its "Done when" passes.

**Product.** Mobile-first PWA for two English-speaking parents and their daughter Yana (CE1, French school). Jobs: catch school messages (Telegram + email) so both parents see them; turn them into a calendar, to-dos, and a nightly helper plan; help Yana with homework and French through Mochi (a fat white cat), games, and stories. Parents see English; Yana sees French (parents can switch her to English).

**Stack.** Next.js 14+ App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, Framer Motion, shadcn/ui (parent side only), Supabase (Auth, Postgres + RLS, Storage, pg_cron), Gemini Flash server-side only, Telegram Bot API, web push, Vercel. Free tiers only. Record limits in `docs/limits.md`.

**Hard rules.**
1. Nothing is lost or hidden before both parents tick it. No DELETE on `messages`. Archive only when every parent has ticked, enforced in SQL (`archive_message`).
2. Gemini is server-side only. Validate output with zod before storing. Compute maths answers in code. Strip names, school name, and addresses before any Gemini call.
3. Mochi never chats freely. Lines come from a scripted FR/EN phrase library. Gemini never speaks to the child.
4. Photos, voice, and family images stay in private storage with RLS. Never send them to an AI unless a parent chose to process that item.
5. No ads, trackers, analytics SDKs, dark patterns, lives, or streak guilt. Parents set the daily play cap. Reward effort.
6. Stars change only through the `award_stars` SQL function.
7. Queue every long task in `jobs` (save the original first). Never rely on one long serverless request.
8. Typed everywhere. Tests for the planner, classifier, validators, and SQL functions. `.env.example`, seed script, README. Lint, typecheck, and tests must pass before a step is done.

**Two experiences.** Parent: magic-link email login; tabs Inbox, Calendar, To do, Progress, Setup; English; PIN to enter, lock on leave. Kid mode: same parent session; tabs Home, Homework, Games, Store; PIN to exit (`families.pin_hash`, verified server-side). Kid screens never show the inbox.

**Design.** Plum `#2A0B4A`, grape `#7C3AED`, hot pink `#FF2E93`, sun `#FFD23F`, Fredoka, 56px kid targets, max 3 choices per kid screen, phone portrait and two-pane tablet at 820px+, light/dark, `prefers-reduced-motion`. Match `ui/mochi-app-prototype.html`.

**Mochi.** Layered SVG cat in a salon (window, curtains, sofa, rug, plant, frames, yarn). State machine: `idle`, `wander`, `chase-yarn`, `nap`, `purr`, `cheer`, `think`, `sleepy-at-bedtime`, `greet`. Random idle every 6–7s. Pause when hidden. Eyes follow the pointer. Friend bubble (bunny, panda, fox, corgi, hamster) every ~9s: pop plays a greeting, awards 2 stars, unlocks the friend. Original designs only. Moods map to app events. Outfits live in `child_outfits`.

**Voice.** `speak()` uses `speechSynthesis` (fr-FR or en-US, high pitch, slow rate) only after a user gesture. 🔊/🔇 in `children.settings`; parents can disable voice. Read homework and stories with a per-block button. Yana records with `MediaRecorder` (Safari mime fallback) into the private `voice` bucket. No auto-grading in v1. Keep `speak()` swappable for reviewed audio files later.
